Yeah, well, I suppose, huh?

1288
00:53:53,600 --> 00:53:55,433
I wonder who
they're planning on shooting.

1289
00:53:55,433 --> 00:53:56,667
Listo.

1290
00:53:56,667 --> 00:53:57,667
Mentos.

1291
00:53:57,667 --> 00:53:59,867
Punten.

1292
00:53:59,867 --> 00:54:01,433
Viva Cuba?

1293
00:54:01,433 --> 00:54:02,533
Disparen!

1294
00:54:02,533 --> 00:54:04,133
Pull!
[Gunshots]

1295
00:54:04,133 --> 00:54:06,633
He seems okay with this.

1296
00:54:06,633 --> 00:54:11,033
Missed me, missed me, now you...
Have to... kiss me.

1297
00:54:11,033 --> 00:54:12,567
Ugh.

1298
00:54:16,467 --> 00:54:18,033
So the rest of the movie

1299
00:54:18,033 --> 00:54:20,867
is just watching them all
get shot one by one?

1300
00:54:20,867 --> 00:54:23,433
I may enjoy it.

1301
00:54:23,433 --> 00:54:26,500
You know, Coleman Francis would
make a really lumpy mattress.

1302
00:54:26,500 --> 00:54:27,833
Eww, not that I...

1303
00:54:27,833 --> 00:54:30,933
Would someone please
get me a doctor?

1304
00:54:30,933 --> 00:54:32,967
I'm George takei.

1305
00:54:32,967 --> 00:54:35,367
No doctor
coming here.

1306
00:54:35,367 --> 00:54:37,233
You'll have to sweat it out.

1307
00:54:37,233 --> 00:54:39,333
Nyah, nyah, nyah.

1308
00:54:39,333 --> 00:54:42,867
Managed care at its best.

1309
00:54:42,867 --> 00:54:45,300
Oh, for the love
of Pete.

1310
00:54:51,433 --> 00:54:52,567
Peek-a-boo!

1311
00:54:52,567 --> 00:54:54,433
Who's in there?
Who's in there?

1312
00:54:54,433 --> 00:54:56,467
Mmm, this looks delicious.

1313
00:54:59,367 --> 00:55:01,800
Here,
let Coleman kiss it.

1314
00:55:01,800 --> 00:55:04,767
The tender touch
of Coleman Francis.

1315
00:55:08,333 --> 00:55:10,500
He won't last 24 hours.

1316
00:55:10,500 --> 00:55:13,233
I've seen torn pants
like that before.

1317
00:55:13,233 --> 00:55:14,267
Gangrene.

1318
00:55:14,267 --> 00:55:15,533
Coleman was pre-med.

1319
00:55:15,533 --> 00:55:17,933
Men in prison had it.

1320
00:55:17,933 --> 00:55:19,967
The doctor didn't
get to 'em in time.

1321
00:55:19,967 --> 00:55:22,333
Somebody get me some water.

1322
00:55:22,333 --> 00:55:24,367
I'm dying in a rush.

1323
00:55:27,767 --> 00:55:29,500
I don't know much
about executions,

1324
00:55:29,500 --> 00:55:32,500
but maybe they could
shoot two at a time, hmm?

1325
00:55:32,500 --> 00:55:34,267
The other two guys
went on break.

1326
00:55:34,267 --> 00:55:35,767
I'm gonna solo on this one.

1327
00:55:35,767 --> 00:55:37,367
No? Okay, fine.

1328
00:55:38,667 --> 00:55:40,100
Listo...

1329
00:55:40,100 --> 00:55:43,667
They actually made it
a fairly challenging shot.

1330
00:55:43,667 --> 00:55:45,133
I've got a very delicate
kidney.

1331
00:55:45,133 --> 00:55:46,133
Disparen!

1332
00:55:46,133 --> 00:55:47,300
[Gunshots]

1333
00:55:47,300 --> 00:55:49,500
Oh, that's great.

1334
00:55:49,500 --> 00:55:52,267
[Chuckles]

1335
00:55:52,267 --> 00:55:53,367
[Laughter]

1336
00:55:53,367 --> 00:55:54,433
Well.

1337
00:55:57,200 --> 00:55:58,133
Bye.

1338
00:55:59,833 --> 00:56:02,233
Curious George goes to Cuba.

1339
00:56:06,100 --> 00:56:07,867
Hey, that's the guy
who just got shot!

1340
00:56:09,567 --> 00:56:10,767
Hey, we're next.

1341
00:56:10,767 --> 00:56:11,800
He butted.

1342
00:56:11,800 --> 00:56:13,167
Must be midnight.

1343
00:56:13,167 --> 00:56:15,600
We're gonna let it
all hang down.

1344
00:56:15,600 --> 00:56:17,200
[Speaking Spanish]

1345
00:56:17,200 --> 00:56:19,167
Wah-wah-wah-wah-wah-wah.

1346
00:56:19,167 --> 00:56:20,467
Wah-wah-wah, wah.

1347
00:56:20,467 --> 00:56:23,233
They change guards
at midnight.

1348
00:56:23,233 --> 00:56:26,233
And they do
light gardening at midnight.

1349
00:56:29,800 --> 00:56:32,533
This is getting to be
a drag, guys.

1350
00:56:36,133 --> 00:56:38,900
Will somebody
get me some water?

1351
00:56:38,900 --> 00:56:41,667
I shot a man
at the Mexican border.

1352
00:56:41,667 --> 00:56:43,800
Go to the window.

1353
00:56:43,800 --> 00:56:47,000
Ask the guard if a wounded man
can have some water.

1354
00:56:47,000 --> 00:56:48,467
I think it'll be funny.

1355
00:56:48,467 --> 00:56:50,100
If they give you some,

1356
00:56:50,100 --> 00:56:52,300
then we have a chance
to make a break.

1357
00:56:52,300 --> 00:56:54,333
They won't give us none.

1358
00:56:54,333 --> 00:56:56,367
They know we're all
starving for water.

1359
00:56:56,367 --> 00:56:58,167
Tell the guard
he's got a fever.

1360
00:56:58,167 --> 00:56:59,233
Go on, try it.

1361
00:57:01,767 --> 00:57:06,233
Oh, and, uh,
take your time.

1362
00:57:06,233 --> 00:57:07,233
Guard!

1363
00:57:07,233 --> 00:57:09,867
- It's me, Margaret.
- Sentry.

1364
00:57:09,867 --> 00:57:10,933
Water.

1365
00:57:10,933 --> 00:57:11,967
[Snickers]

1366
00:57:11,967 --> 00:57:13,167
Man's got a fever.

1367
00:57:13,167 --> 00:57:15,300
He got boogie fever.

1368
00:57:15,300 --> 00:57:17,067
Just a cupful.

1369
00:57:17,067 --> 00:57:20,967
Well, they got a south-facing
cell, that's nice.

1370
00:57:20,967 --> 00:57:22,167
I don't have any water.

1371
00:57:22,167 --> 00:57:23,900
I've got
a wonderful bouillon here.

1372
00:57:23,900 --> 00:57:26,367
I know, I just got killed.
I get that a lot.

1373
00:57:28,933 --> 00:57:31,400
I hate these prisons where you
gotta ask for water.

1374
00:57:31,400 --> 00:57:34,767
Why don't they just bring it
to the table?

1375
00:57:34,767 --> 00:57:37,000
It's not without its charm.

1376
00:57:40,400 --> 00:57:43,267
Well, hey, this has little
marshmallows in it.

1377
00:57:46,033 --> 00:57:47,500
What'd, it come
out of a magician's kit?

1378
00:57:47,500 --> 00:57:48,700
It's bottomless.

1379
00:57:48,700 --> 00:57:51,467
Hey, he's double-dipping!

1380
00:57:54,400 --> 00:57:57,233
Thanks, guys,
the backwash really helps.

1381
00:57:59,633 --> 00:58:01,967
I just gotta look
in the girls' cabin.

1382
00:58:01,967 --> 00:58:03,733
Eh-- ooh, no.

1383
00:58:03,733 --> 00:58:05,933
Have to control myself.
Control.

1384
00:58:05,933 --> 00:58:08,800
Mm, be strong.

1385
00:58:08,800 --> 00:58:10,800
That water plan
really went wrong.

1386
00:58:10,800 --> 00:58:12,467
Tomorrow night at midnight,

1387
00:58:12,467 --> 00:58:15,200
after they change guards,

1388
00:58:15,200 --> 00:58:17,733
one guard
will be out front.

1389
00:58:17,733 --> 00:58:20,833
The other one
walks around the hut,

1390
00:58:20,833 --> 00:58:22,833
when the guard out front
is alone.

1391
00:58:22,833 --> 00:58:24,267
No, nothing's sinking in.

1392
00:58:24,267 --> 00:58:26,233
Ask him for water.

1393
00:58:26,233 --> 00:58:28,533
It's gotta work this time.

1394
00:58:28,533 --> 00:58:30,633
Castro looks like
Toulouse-lautrec.

1395
00:58:30,633 --> 00:58:32,200
[Laughing]

1396
00:58:32,200 --> 00:58:34,300
Why'd they bring
dian fossey?

1397
00:58:37,167 --> 00:58:41,133
Ah, fidel had to go
potty behind a tree.

1398
00:58:41,133 --> 00:58:43,233
We'd better move out now.

1399
00:58:43,233 --> 00:58:44,533
He's here again.

1400
00:58:44,533 --> 00:58:45,733
Hmm?

1401
00:58:45,733 --> 00:58:47,767
The airstrip we passed
when they captured us.

1402
00:58:47,767 --> 00:58:49,667
Can you handle
one of those planes?

1403
00:58:49,667 --> 00:58:50,933
I can handle it.

1404
00:58:50,933 --> 00:58:53,133
I was in skydivers,
you know.

1405
00:58:58,800 --> 00:58:59,900
Cook.

1406
00:58:59,900 --> 00:59:01,633
That's the county
Chicago's in.

1407
00:59:01,633 --> 00:59:03,000
Ask the guard
for some water.

1408
00:59:03,000 --> 00:59:04,600
The movie lapped itself.

1409
00:59:04,600 --> 00:59:07,800
If he brings it to you,
I'll be at the window.

1410
00:59:07,800 --> 00:59:10,033
Make him
move in close.

1411
00:59:10,033 --> 00:59:11,533
How will I know you?

1412
00:59:11,533 --> 00:59:14,433
If I can get
my hands on him,

1413
00:59:14,433 --> 00:59:16,267
I'll snap his neck.

1414
00:59:16,267 --> 00:59:18,533
Don't we wait
for the guard change?

1415
00:59:18,533 --> 00:59:20,267
We've got to make it now.

1416
00:59:20,267 --> 00:59:24,600
That airstrip--
two, maybe three miles.

1417
00:59:24,600 --> 00:59:26,200
You have to give me time
to check.

1418
00:59:26,200 --> 00:59:28,200
We need a plane
that's got enough gas.

1419
00:59:28,200 --> 00:59:30,533
Take me with you.

1420
00:59:30,533 --> 00:59:32,900
It's about that time.

1421
00:59:32,900 --> 00:59:34,200
That ranch
I told you about.

1422
00:59:34,200 --> 00:59:35,833
It's got a mountain
of pitchblende.

1423
00:59:35,833 --> 00:59:38,033
They're practically
giving it away!

1424
00:59:38,033 --> 00:59:40,833
Uranium, tungsten--
diamonds, maybe.

1425
00:59:40,833 --> 00:59:44,167
Now, look, you've got a busted
leg, and we can't carry you.

1426
00:59:44,167 --> 00:59:45,333
I've had it with you!

1427
00:59:45,333 --> 00:59:47,133
I'll carry myself.

1428
00:59:50,200 --> 00:59:53,400
What kind of a cock-and-bull
story you laying on us?

1429
00:59:53,400 --> 00:59:55,267
I'm a bad boy.

1430
00:59:55,267 --> 00:59:57,467
There's riches
on my mountain.

1431
00:59:57,467 --> 00:59:58,667
Uranium.

1432
00:59:58,667 --> 01:00:00,000
The tension mounts.

1433
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:02,400
Tungsten, worth thousands.

1434
01:00:02,400 --> 01:00:04,500
Ma-maybe even hundreds.

1435
01:00:04,500 --> 01:00:06,933
I-I know
it sounds crazy...

1436
01:00:06,933 --> 01:00:08,533
But would you choke me again?

1437
01:00:08,533 --> 01:00:09,533
... but I believe him.

1438
01:00:09,533 --> 01:00:10,967
What you talkin' 'bout,
Willis?

1439
01:00:10,967 --> 01:00:14,300
Griffin,
let's go to Arizona.

1440
01:00:14,300 --> 01:00:18,300
I was just beginning to enjoy
new Mexico-slash-Cuba.

1441
01:00:18,300 --> 01:00:19,933
Check the window.

1442
01:00:19,933 --> 01:00:22,933
And ask the guard for
some water, what the heck.

1443
01:00:22,933 --> 01:00:24,833
He's crazy enough
to do it.

1444
01:00:24,833 --> 01:00:26,933
He's gonna check the window!

1445
01:00:26,933 --> 01:00:29,700
Look at that big old hair grease
stain they're leaving there.

1446
01:00:29,700 --> 01:00:31,333
Ugh.

1447
01:00:31,333 --> 01:00:34,200
Is the film grainy, or are
these guys just kind of grainy?

1448
01:00:34,200 --> 01:00:36,533
Water... thirsty.

1449
01:00:36,533 --> 01:00:37,733
Sick man.

1450
01:00:37,733 --> 01:00:39,000
Uh, things you'd say
to a guard!

1451
01:00:39,000 --> 01:00:40,000
Uh, things in a prison!

1452
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:42,433
Pass, pass...

1453
01:00:42,433 --> 01:00:45,700
I don't think
he's going to buy it.

1454
01:00:45,700 --> 01:00:46,967
Ask him again.

1455
01:00:46,967 --> 01:00:48,733
Come on, improvise a little.

1456
01:00:48,733 --> 01:00:49,900
Water!

1457
01:00:49,900 --> 01:00:51,933
Thirsty.
Sick man.

1458
01:00:51,933 --> 01:00:53,233
Uh, things you get
from a tap.

1459
01:00:53,233 --> 01:00:54,267
Things you
call your grandpa.

1460
01:00:54,267 --> 01:00:56,233
Things you--
oh, move on, please!

1461
01:01:00,300 --> 01:01:01,900
Water.

1462
01:01:01,900 --> 01:01:04,533
Oh, please,
I'm not a huggy person-- agh!

1463
01:01:04,533 --> 01:01:07,033
He's dead already,
so it's a lot easier.

1464
01:01:07,033 --> 01:01:10,333
♪♪

1465
01:01:10,333 --> 01:01:12,800
Oh, the jumping training
pays off.

1466
01:01:12,800 --> 01:01:13,933
I stand corrected.

1467
01:01:13,933 --> 01:01:15,367
[Giggles]

1468
01:01:15,367 --> 01:01:16,667
Huh? What the--

1469
01:01:16,667 --> 01:01:17,667
[laughter]

1470
01:01:17,667 --> 01:01:19,500
Escape from "green acres."

1471
01:01:19,500 --> 01:01:22,500
[Shouting in Spanish]

1472
01:01:22,500 --> 01:01:23,600
♪♪

1473
01:01:23,600 --> 01:01:25,333
Achtung!
I mean, allons-y!

1474
01:01:25,333 --> 01:01:26,567
Uh, zut alors!

1475
01:01:26,567 --> 01:01:29,233
Wait, i'm...

1476
01:01:29,233 --> 01:01:31,533
Oh, it's daytime now.

1477
01:01:31,533 --> 01:01:34,733
Hee hee, well, they ran
into ye olde mining town.

1478
01:01:34,733 --> 01:01:35,833
[Gunshot]

1479
01:01:35,833 --> 01:01:37,833
Water... thirsty.

1480
01:01:37,833 --> 01:01:38,933
Sick man.

1481
01:01:38,933 --> 01:01:40,933
It's nighttime again.

1482
01:01:40,933 --> 01:01:42,233
And day.

1483
01:01:42,233 --> 01:01:45,467
♪ Night and day,
da da da da ♪

1484
01:01:47,867 --> 01:01:49,400
[Whimpers]

1485
01:01:49,400 --> 01:01:51,533
The airstrip˯ oughta be
over that way.

1486
01:01:51,533 --> 01:01:52,833
Let's go.

1487
01:01:52,833 --> 01:01:54,700
The bronko nagurski gang!

1488
01:01:54,700 --> 01:01:56,833
[Laughing]

1489
01:01:56,833 --> 01:02:00,733
[Humming]

1490
01:02:00,733 --> 01:02:03,100
[Whistling]

1491
01:02:03,100 --> 01:02:06,367
Join me and Che Guevara
as we go hunting mercenaries.

1492
01:02:13,233 --> 01:02:15,900
♪ Hello muddah, faddah ♪

1493
01:02:15,900 --> 01:02:18,333
Yep, I'm Cuban.

1494
01:02:18,333 --> 01:02:20,300
Huh?
I mean, 'Kay.

1495
01:02:22,867 --> 01:02:24,667
[Speaking French]

1496
01:02:24,667 --> 01:02:26,267
Uh, uh... oh.

1497
01:02:26,267 --> 01:02:29,500
Today's guard
wears stylish flairs.

1498
01:02:31,900 --> 01:02:33,433
Actionlessness!

1499
01:02:35,267 --> 01:02:36,433
Ah, whew!

1500
01:02:36,433 --> 01:02:37,600
I wasn't that close, huh?

1501
01:02:41,400 --> 01:02:42,567
Well, that one's okay.

1502
01:02:42,567 --> 01:02:45,033
I'm not wild
about the interior.

1503
01:02:45,033 --> 01:02:47,567
I turned everything on--
the radio, the lights.

1504
01:02:47,567 --> 01:02:49,833
Ah.

1505
01:02:49,833 --> 01:02:53,167
Darn good thing they escaped
during the Cuban aircraft expo.

1506
01:02:54,333 --> 01:02:57,833
Look at him run,
the little femme.

1507
01:02:57,833 --> 01:03:00,933
Look, peanuts aren't important--
just take one!

1508
01:03:00,933 --> 01:03:04,500
A fortune in pitch blend
is riding on this scene.

1509
01:03:04,500 --> 01:03:07,467
I'm gonna put my wig on,
see if that helps any.

1510
01:03:07,467 --> 01:03:08,567
That's good.

1511
01:03:08,567 --> 01:03:09,567
Huh?

1512
01:03:09,567 --> 01:03:11,833
♪♪

1513
01:03:11,833 --> 01:03:13,600
[Chuckling]

1514
01:03:13,600 --> 01:03:15,333
Good, Rick.

1515
01:03:15,333 --> 01:03:17,300
Uh, "d" for drive...

1516
01:03:17,300 --> 01:03:19,000
"F" must mean fly, hmm.

1517
01:03:19,000 --> 01:03:20,967
Let's go.

1518
01:03:20,967 --> 01:03:23,500
♪♪

1519
01:03:23,500 --> 01:03:26,933
He's using
Coleman's slipstream.

1520
01:03:26,933 --> 01:03:28,133
Well...

1521
01:03:28,133 --> 01:03:30,100
Oh, please, I'm in enough
trouble already!

1522
01:03:31,900 --> 01:03:34,500
Fuzzy thurston
is the fugitive!

1523
01:03:34,500 --> 01:03:35,500
[Laughing]

1524
01:03:35,500 --> 01:03:36,967
Hey, moe, moe!

1525
01:03:36,967 --> 01:03:39,433
Let go of the camera!
Please go!

1526
01:03:39,433 --> 01:03:41,967
Wub-wub-wub-wub-wub-wub-wub!
Ngh, ngh, ngh, ngh!

1527
01:03:44,100 --> 01:03:45,300
- Oh...
- Helping?

1528
01:03:45,300 --> 01:03:47,000
- No, not at all.
- Hmm.

1529
01:03:47,000 --> 01:03:48,467
They look cute.

1530
01:03:48,467 --> 01:03:51,633
Those whitewalls really kind of
screw up the camouflage, huh?

1531
01:03:51,633 --> 01:03:52,800
♪♪

1532
01:03:52,800 --> 01:03:55,333
[Engine puttering]

1533
01:03:57,100 --> 01:03:59,300
[Coughing]

1534
01:03:59,300 --> 01:04:01,667
You know, I still like this
movie better than "Havana."

1535
01:04:01,667 --> 01:04:02,667
Oh, yeah.

1536
01:04:02,667 --> 01:04:04,533
[Gunshots]

1537
01:04:04,533 --> 01:04:08,133
Oh...
[Grunting]

1538
01:04:08,133 --> 01:04:10,667
Come on, you guys, my boss
is gonna be really mad!

1539
01:04:12,700 --> 01:04:14,233
What?

1540
01:04:14,233 --> 01:04:15,733
[Gunshots]

1541
01:04:15,733 --> 01:04:17,100
All right, tay!

1542
01:04:21,367 --> 01:04:24,733
Pull... pull...
Pull!

1543
01:04:24,733 --> 01:04:26,200
♪♪

1544
01:04:26,200 --> 01:04:29,133
[Gunfire]

1545
01:04:31,200 --> 01:04:33,267
Just ignore them,
rise above it.

1546
01:04:34,800 --> 01:04:35,967
Whoo, whew!

1547
01:04:35,967 --> 01:04:38,300
Boy, that was close.
They made it, though.

1548
01:04:38,300 --> 01:04:40,967
Next, we visit
lovely busch gardens.

1549
01:04:40,967 --> 01:04:44,000
Well, in some parts of Cuba,
it was a nice day.

1550
01:04:44,000 --> 01:04:46,233
Stay off the road
and keep your eyes open.

1551
01:04:46,233 --> 01:04:49,400
If you see anything, film--
I will put it in.

1552
01:04:52,667 --> 01:04:56,733
Coleman, are we still
in a plane in Cuba?

1553
01:04:56,733 --> 01:05:01,200
It's all an elaborate plan
to find a nice picnic spot.

1554
01:05:01,200 --> 01:05:04,267
They should have tried to take
over Belize or grand Cayman.

1555
01:05:04,267 --> 01:05:06,633
Would have been easier
for their first time.

1556
01:05:06,633 --> 01:05:08,267
Huh, so that's tungsten.

1557
01:05:08,267 --> 01:05:09,767
Thought it
would be cooler.

1558
01:05:12,300 --> 01:05:14,567
Whoa, little dog poopy there.

1559
01:05:18,133 --> 01:05:20,433
Under the spreading
Coleman Francis,

1560
01:05:20,433 --> 01:05:23,200
the village smithy stands.

1561
01:05:23,200 --> 01:05:26,433
It says,
"viva frogs' legs."

1562
01:05:26,433 --> 01:05:30,233
Ohh, man, don't tempt me.
Mmm.

1563
01:05:30,233 --> 01:05:33,367
Is that the lunch wall
or the dinner wall?

1564
01:05:33,367 --> 01:05:37,300
I am the dark specter
of food.

1565
01:05:37,300 --> 01:05:40,267
I sensed there was mail.

1566
01:05:40,267 --> 01:05:43,067
I have a frog leg place
over there.

1567
01:05:43,067 --> 01:05:45,233
Great,
my "wall street journal."

1568
01:05:45,233 --> 01:05:46,300
[Sniffing]
Uhh!

1569
01:05:46,300 --> 01:05:48,633
Whoa!
Gave myself a snuggie there.

1570
01:05:48,633 --> 01:05:51,200
Frog legs...
Let's get us some!

1571
01:05:56,133 --> 01:05:59,033
I gotta get me
a mechanical bull.

1572
01:06:00,800 --> 01:06:02,333
[Sighs]

1573
01:06:02,333 --> 01:06:04,433
Location, location,
location.

1574
01:06:04,433 --> 01:06:07,800
Just look at that
curb appeal, huh?

1575
01:06:07,800 --> 01:06:10,933
♪♪ [Piano playing]

1576
01:06:10,933 --> 01:06:13,333
You think
I'm dressed for it?

1577
01:06:13,333 --> 01:06:15,433
[Chuckles]

1578
01:06:15,433 --> 01:06:18,200
My name is death.
I'll be your waiter.

1579
01:06:18,200 --> 01:06:19,567
What can I do for you, boys?

1580
01:06:19,567 --> 01:06:22,533
Do you have
any catfish?

1581
01:06:22,533 --> 01:06:23,967
Coffee.

1582
01:06:23,967 --> 01:06:25,000
Coffee coming up.

1583
01:06:25,000 --> 01:06:27,933
Ah, coffee,
a Coleman Francis motif.

1584
01:06:27,933 --> 01:06:30,533
The kitchen guy
just died, sorry.

1585
01:06:30,533 --> 01:06:34,767
My father was a can opener,
and my mother was a wood duck.

1586
01:06:36,333 --> 01:06:38,967
A pie doesn't make you
want to kill yourself.

1587
01:06:38,967 --> 01:06:40,300
You want some?

1588
01:06:40,300 --> 01:06:43,800
Who's playing that piano?

1589
01:06:43,800 --> 01:06:45,167
That's my daughter.

1590
01:06:45,167 --> 01:06:48,833
She's wed
to the devil.

1591
01:06:48,833 --> 01:06:50,600
She's been blind,
you know,

1592
01:06:50,600 --> 01:06:53,300
since her husband
got killed in the war.

1593
01:06:53,300 --> 01:06:55,300
That makes sense.

1594
01:06:55,300 --> 01:06:56,767
We got an omelet called

1595
01:06:56,767 --> 01:06:59,200
"supercalifragilistic-
expial-delicious."

1596
01:06:59,200 --> 01:07:01,367
Doctors have done
everything for her.

1597
01:07:01,367 --> 01:07:03,567
- Tried glasses?
- Nothing.

1598
01:07:03,567 --> 01:07:04,667
Spent all of my money.

1599
01:07:04,667 --> 01:07:06,333
Sure, we're gonna
put her down.

1600
01:07:06,333 --> 01:07:10,267
Since that freeway went in,
lost all our business.

1601
01:07:10,267 --> 01:07:12,433
I guess
it's not much use trying.

1602
01:07:12,433 --> 01:07:13,500
[Sighs]

1603
01:07:13,500 --> 01:07:15,567
May as well fold up
and pull out.

1604
01:07:15,567 --> 01:07:18,433
But I have my health,
and my spirits are high.

1605
01:07:18,433 --> 01:07:21,433
We have a wonderful
oktoberfest frog leg.

1606
01:07:24,600 --> 01:07:27,600
♪♪

1607
01:07:27,600 --> 01:07:29,567
Sitting in on chifforobe.

1608
01:07:29,567 --> 01:07:31,033
[Laughing]

1609
01:07:31,033 --> 01:07:32,600
You see,
they're just jealous.

1610
01:07:32,600 --> 01:07:34,433
He was showing off,
well, with his daughter

1611
01:07:34,433 --> 01:07:36,367
and his ritzy restaurant
and all.

1612
01:07:36,367 --> 01:07:38,433
♪♪

1613
01:07:38,433 --> 01:07:41,433
Whoo! Surprisingly quick out of
the blocks, this fellow.

1614
01:07:41,433 --> 01:07:42,867
[Chuckles]
Okay, slow down.

1615
01:07:42,867 --> 01:07:44,167
Speed up.
Slow down.

1616
01:07:44,167 --> 01:07:46,833
♪♪

1617
01:07:46,833 --> 01:07:51,333
You and your swank restaurant
and your chichi frog legs!

1618
01:07:51,333 --> 01:07:53,767
Suppose you boys'll
be wanting your check.

1619
01:07:53,767 --> 01:07:55,833
Oh!

1620
01:07:55,833 --> 01:07:58,100
I'm gonna have to ask you
to leave if this continues.

1621
01:07:58,100 --> 01:07:59,600
Ow!

1622
01:08:01,967 --> 01:08:04,100
"Apple's way" is different
than I remember.

1623
01:08:04,100 --> 01:08:05,400
[Giggles]

1624
01:08:06,967 --> 01:08:09,533
Now, where in Cuba do you
suppose they are?

1625
01:08:15,833 --> 01:08:17,967
Not the frog mine, no!

1626
01:08:17,967 --> 01:08:19,567
Eh, heh,
I kind of like it.

1627
01:08:19,567 --> 01:08:20,633
Saddle me up, boys!

1628
01:08:20,633 --> 01:08:28,233
Aaaaaah...

1629
01:08:28,233 --> 01:08:32,933
Ohh...

1630
01:08:32,933 --> 01:08:35,500
Splash!

1631
01:08:35,500 --> 01:08:39,433
There, now we have the rest
of the day to ourselves.

1632
01:08:39,433 --> 01:08:43,900
♪♪ [Woman singing soprano]

1633
01:08:43,900 --> 01:08:46,800
The legendary
singing buick!

1634
01:08:46,800 --> 01:08:49,733
How are they gonna get the car
down a well?

1635
01:08:49,733 --> 01:08:51,900
Check that junk box,
see if it'll run.

1636
01:08:51,900 --> 01:08:53,567
All right.

1637
01:08:53,567 --> 01:08:58,233
I just keep thinking
of those tasty frog legs.

1638
01:08:58,233 --> 01:09:01,367
Ah, home of the famous
steak ala weismeyer.

1639
01:09:01,367 --> 01:09:03,967
The lure of the siren.

1640
01:09:03,967 --> 01:09:07,367
♪♪ [Piano playing]

1641
01:09:07,367 --> 01:09:09,400
♪♪ [Singing continues]

1642
01:09:09,400 --> 01:09:13,300
I heartily endorse
throwing her down a well.

1643
01:09:13,300 --> 01:09:15,300
Hey look, tab hunter
lives here.

1644
01:09:15,300 --> 01:09:16,867
What do you know.

1645
01:09:16,867 --> 01:09:19,333
You know, the freeway
may not be the problem.

1646
01:09:19,333 --> 01:09:21,200
Yeah.

1647
01:09:21,200 --> 01:09:23,133
♪♪

1648
01:09:36,867 --> 01:09:38,467
Forget that,
where did he get the wig?

1649
01:09:38,467 --> 01:09:40,300
Oh, hi, Ms. Channing!

1650
01:09:40,300 --> 01:09:41,400
What's new?

1651
01:09:41,400 --> 01:09:43,433
Oh, I'm not Carol Channing.

1652
01:09:43,433 --> 01:09:45,567
Oh, thank goodness,
Mike.

1653
01:09:45,567 --> 01:09:46,567
You must be feeling
a little bit--

1654
01:09:46,567 --> 01:09:47,567
I'm t-bone Burnett.

1655
01:09:47,567 --> 01:09:49,100
Uh-huh.

1656
01:09:49,100 --> 01:09:51,333
That's not right either.
Hold on.

1657
01:09:51,333 --> 01:09:52,467
I'm Vicki Lawrence.

1658
01:09:52,467 --> 01:09:54,067
Eh, uh...

1659
01:09:54,067 --> 01:09:55,867
[Sighs]
Then again...

1660
01:09:55,867 --> 01:09:58,067
Maybe I should just go
lie down for a while.

1661
01:09:58,067 --> 01:09:59,800
- That's a great idea, honey.
- Yeah, bye-bye.

1662
01:09:59,800 --> 01:10:00,933
You lie down.

1663
01:10:00,933 --> 01:10:02,167
It's the movie,
don't worry, okay?

1664
01:10:02,167 --> 01:10:03,267
It'll be just fine.

1665
01:10:03,267 --> 01:10:04,700
We better check
on his nibs.

1666
01:10:04,700 --> 01:10:05,900
Oh, yeah, right.

1667
01:10:05,900 --> 01:10:09,167
♪ It's a marshmallow world
in the winter ♪

1668
01:10:09,167 --> 01:10:11,233
No, those are my pants!

1669
01:10:11,233 --> 01:10:13,833
Quigley down under, help me!
Help!

1670
01:10:13,833 --> 01:10:17,333
There, there, Dr. F.
There, there.

1671
01:10:17,333 --> 01:10:19,967
Well, Mike,
it's not looking good.

1672
01:10:19,967 --> 01:10:22,300
I'm afraid we may
be at the end.

1673
01:10:22,300 --> 01:10:24,100
- Frank?
- Yes?

1674
01:10:24,100 --> 01:10:25,100
Frank.

1675
01:10:25,100 --> 01:10:26,100
Yes, Dr. F.?

1676
01:10:26,100 --> 01:10:27,900
- Frank!
- I'm right here, Dr. F.

1677
01:10:27,900 --> 01:10:29,267
- Frank?
- What?

1678
01:10:29,267 --> 01:10:30,900
- Frank!
- Yes, Dr. F.

1679
01:10:30,900 --> 01:10:31,933
- Frank!
- What?!

1680
01:10:31,933 --> 01:10:35,200
Frank, I'm going down
a long hallway.

1681
01:10:35,200 --> 01:10:38,333
There's a figure
at the end beckoning to me.

1682
01:10:38,333 --> 01:10:41,300
Well, don't you think you ought
to go to him then, doctor?

1683
01:10:41,300 --> 01:10:45,067
Frank... there's something
I've always wanted to tell you.

1684
01:10:45,067 --> 01:10:48,067
Look, let's not make
a big production out of this.

1685
01:10:48,067 --> 01:10:49,500
There's a guy
down at the end of the hallway

1686
01:10:49,500 --> 01:10:50,900
waiting for you, okay?

1687
01:10:50,900 --> 01:10:54,067
Yes, he's tapping his foot
and looking at his watch.

1688
01:10:54,067 --> 01:10:57,167
Well, don't you think
you ought to go to him, then?

1689
01:10:57,167 --> 01:11:00,067
[Grunting]

1690
01:11:00,067 --> 01:11:01,633
Oh, frank...

1691
01:11:01,633 --> 01:11:03,300
- Yes?
- This is it.

1692
01:11:03,300 --> 01:11:05,167
I--

1693
01:11:05,167 --> 01:11:07,433
hyah.

1694
01:11:07,433 --> 01:11:10,900
And... it is done.

1695
01:11:12,633 --> 01:11:14,867
Dr. Clayton.

1696
01:11:14,867 --> 01:11:16,967
No, wait.

1697
01:11:16,967 --> 01:11:18,800
I'm alive.

1698
01:11:18,800 --> 01:11:19,833
No.

1699
01:11:19,833 --> 01:11:21,833
I'm dead.

1700
01:11:21,833 --> 01:11:23,633
No.

1701
01:11:23,633 --> 01:11:24,633
Yes.

1702
01:11:24,633 --> 01:11:26,667
No.

1703
01:11:26,667 --> 01:11:28,800
Now I'm dead.

1704
01:11:28,800 --> 01:11:30,633
Wait.

1705
01:11:30,633 --> 01:11:32,867
I'm still alive.

1706
01:11:32,867 --> 01:11:34,667
No.

1707
01:11:34,667 --> 01:11:37,533
I'm dead.

1708
01:11:37,533 --> 01:11:38,700
Wait.

1709
01:11:38,700 --> 01:11:40,867
I can't die.

1710
01:11:40,867 --> 01:11:42,633
I've got too much
to live for.

1711
01:11:42,633 --> 01:11:45,100
[Fabric ripping]
I've got my good friend frank.

1712
01:11:45,100 --> 01:11:47,133
I've got... things!

1713
01:11:47,133 --> 01:11:50,367
Uh, things
that I gotta... do!

1714
01:11:50,367 --> 01:11:52,867
I gotta live and laugh
and love

1715
01:11:52,867 --> 01:11:55,967
and live
and embrace the world!

1716
01:11:55,967 --> 01:11:57,600
I wanna live!

1717
01:11:57,600 --> 01:11:59,567
Ohh! Joe!

1718
01:11:59,567 --> 01:12:00,667
Hi!

1719
01:12:00,667 --> 01:12:03,200
[Grunting, impact blows]

1720
01:12:03,200 --> 01:12:04,700
That hurt!

1721
01:12:04,700 --> 01:12:06,733
Ohh! Ooh hoo!

1722
01:12:12,033 --> 01:12:13,367
How you doing, better?

1723
01:12:13,367 --> 01:12:14,833
It still hurts.

1724
01:12:14,833 --> 01:12:16,767
♪♪

1725
01:12:16,767 --> 01:12:18,933
Should have had
those frog legs.

1726
01:12:18,933 --> 01:12:21,167
Pull over.

1727
01:12:21,167 --> 01:12:22,367
Get that top up.

1728
01:12:22,367 --> 01:12:24,833
Coleman, you brat!

1729
01:12:28,033 --> 01:12:30,433
Chinese fire drill.

1730
01:12:32,767 --> 01:12:36,200
So, the frog legs
were real good, huh, guys?

1731
01:12:36,200 --> 01:12:39,067
This is cinema verite
to the ultimate.

1732
01:12:39,067 --> 01:12:42,867
You know, your everyday
annoyances should not be filmed.

1733
01:12:42,867 --> 01:12:44,933
[Wind whistling]

1734
01:12:44,933 --> 01:12:47,767
Hey guys, I'm gonna
change the tape, 'Kay?

1735
01:12:47,767 --> 01:12:50,767
'Kay?
'Kay?

1736
01:12:50,767 --> 01:12:52,200
When we get this top up,

1737
01:12:52,200 --> 01:12:57,767
we're gonna drive back to Cuba
and do it right this time.

1738
01:12:57,767 --> 01:12:58,900
Aha.

1739
01:12:58,900 --> 01:13:01,100
Spend it at cliff weismeyer's!

1740
01:13:02,967 --> 01:13:03,967
Thanks, that helps.

1741
01:13:03,967 --> 01:13:05,367
I was getting cold.

1742
01:13:07,267 --> 01:13:11,267
[Humming]

1743
01:13:11,267 --> 01:13:12,833
♪♪

1744
01:13:12,833 --> 01:13:16,800
Ooh, there's that new overpass
I was telling you about.

1745
01:13:16,800 --> 01:13:19,333
So the Cuban stuff,
just a digression.

1746
01:13:19,333 --> 01:13:20,900
Now the movie
can really begin.

1747
01:13:20,900 --> 01:13:23,100
- Yeah.
- Would you stop?

1748
01:13:23,100 --> 01:13:27,233
♪♪

1749
01:13:27,233 --> 01:13:31,333
Remember when everyone started
dressing like these guys?

1750
01:13:31,333 --> 01:13:32,833
Excuse me, is this the...

1751
01:13:32,833 --> 01:13:37,433
♪ Night train
to mundo fine ♪

1752
01:13:37,433 --> 01:13:38,600
[Laughter]

1753
01:13:38,600 --> 01:13:42,800
Hmm, carradine tracks--
two, three days old.

1754
01:13:42,800 --> 01:13:45,467
They've stumbled
into the end of "mod squad"!

1755
01:13:45,467 --> 01:13:48,400
♪♪

1756
01:13:48,400 --> 01:13:50,800
[Humming]

1757
01:13:50,800 --> 01:13:55,133
♪ Night train to mundo fine ♪

1758
01:13:55,133 --> 01:13:56,600
♪ hey, hey, hey, yeah ♪

1759
01:13:56,600 --> 01:13:58,100
We're gonna let
the air out of the tires.

1760
01:13:58,100 --> 01:13:59,167
[Laughing]

1761
01:13:59,167 --> 01:14:01,967
Hey, Griffin,
the train's moving out.

1762
01:14:01,967 --> 01:14:03,733
Come on, landis,
grab the front end.

1763
01:14:03,733 --> 01:14:05,500
Come on, cook, let's go.

1764
01:14:05,500 --> 01:14:07,800
What the--
what was wrong with the car?

1765
01:14:07,800 --> 01:14:09,467
They had a perfectly
good car.

1766
01:14:09,467 --> 01:14:12,133
All right, go on up.

1767
01:14:12,133 --> 01:14:16,067
All this to get
to the hobo gathering.

1768
01:14:16,067 --> 01:14:17,633
Come on top, cook,
come on.

1769
01:14:17,633 --> 01:14:21,500
I bet they're gonna pistol-whip
Thomas the tank engine.

1770
01:14:21,500 --> 01:14:25,233
This train is bound
for glory, this train...

1771
01:14:25,233 --> 01:14:27,133
[Train whistle blows]

1772
01:14:27,133 --> 01:14:29,133
Shaft did it better.

1773
01:14:29,133 --> 01:14:32,133
I think the club car's
up this way.

1774
01:14:35,067 --> 01:14:36,333
Boy, this movie
doesn't let up.

1775
01:14:36,333 --> 01:14:37,633
Wow.
[Whistles]

1776
01:14:37,633 --> 01:14:40,800
The train-riding sequence
was omitted for clarity.

1777
01:14:43,067 --> 01:14:45,100
I see this as a bed
and breakfast.

1778
01:14:45,100 --> 01:14:46,500
Can you see it?

1779
01:14:46,500 --> 01:14:48,033
We need transportation.

1780
01:14:48,033 --> 01:14:49,267
Yeah.

1781
01:14:49,267 --> 01:14:50,633
We're gonna go legit.

1782
01:14:50,633 --> 01:14:52,633
I'm gonna open
a Claire's boutique.

1783
01:14:52,633 --> 01:14:54,800
I don't want
any more bulls chasing me.

1784
01:14:54,800 --> 01:14:57,200
Landis,
give me the ring.

1785
01:14:57,200 --> 01:15:00,400
That's my Archie
fan club ring.

1786
01:15:00,400 --> 01:15:02,300
I can't
give you this ring.

1787
01:15:02,300 --> 01:15:03,967
My dad gave it to me.

1788
01:15:03,967 --> 01:15:06,400
I don't care if Moses
gave it to you.

1789
01:15:06,400 --> 01:15:08,700
Give me the ring.

1790
01:15:08,700 --> 01:15:11,200
You're not gonna get it.

1791
01:15:11,200 --> 01:15:12,467
[Giggling]

1792
01:15:12,467 --> 01:15:14,300
Oh! Hope that's a gun
he pulled out.

1793
01:15:14,300 --> 01:15:15,400
Uhh!

1794
01:15:18,433 --> 01:15:22,233
Ah, my neck got broken
in that jump cut.

1795
01:15:24,300 --> 01:15:26,600
Well, see, the movie has finally
thrown up its hands

1796
01:15:26,600 --> 01:15:28,800
and said,
"I just don't know."

1797
01:15:28,800 --> 01:15:30,133
I want to hurt this movie,

1798
01:15:30,133 --> 01:15:34,067
but I can never hurt it
the way it hurt me.

1799
01:15:34,067 --> 01:15:37,233
Did they even
need to go to Cuba?

1800
01:15:37,233 --> 01:15:40,433
I was lucky to pick up
one of these rebuilt girls.

1801
01:15:40,433 --> 01:15:43,733
Candy, take the groceries
