01:27:34,233 --> 01:27:38,733
This is a really
stupid use of a split screen.

2061
01:27:38,733 --> 01:27:42,600
Native beaters are used
to flush out the curly.

2062
01:27:44,000 --> 01:27:46,667
Oh, look up there,
it's smelly Kelly in his heli.

2063
01:27:46,667 --> 01:27:48,933
Ah, we're just as good as you,
Kelly!

2064
01:27:50,633 --> 01:27:54,700
Well, I see she bought
more lawn ornaments.

2065
01:27:54,700 --> 01:27:58,267
Got a load of wife for you.

2066
01:27:58,267 --> 01:28:00,500
They shouldn't have skimped
on their privacy fence.

2067
01:28:00,500 --> 01:28:02,833
They hate ankles.

2068
01:28:05,933 --> 01:28:09,200
Great job on the bay of pigs,
honey.

2069
01:28:10,733 --> 01:28:12,567
She's a little
awkward to carry.

2070
01:28:12,567 --> 01:28:15,200
You got a two-Wheeler
in the garage?

2071
01:28:17,267 --> 01:28:18,600
Khh! Oww!

2072
01:28:20,900 --> 01:28:24,133
[Growling]

2073
01:28:24,133 --> 01:28:25,900
And when a curly dies
in the wild,

2074
01:28:25,900 --> 01:28:28,800
he provides food
for other curlys.

2075
01:28:28,800 --> 01:28:30,800
That was him, wasn't it?

2076
01:28:30,800 --> 01:28:32,467
What the hell.

2077
01:28:32,467 --> 01:28:36,600
The cast of "how to succeed
in business" moves in.

2078
01:28:36,600 --> 01:28:39,000
The young, fresh fellows.

2079
01:28:40,667 --> 01:28:42,133
Hard to love
a character for so long

2080
01:28:42,133 --> 01:28:44,667
and to see him come
to such an end.

2081
01:28:44,667 --> 01:28:47,567
Mother of mercy,
is this the end of curly?

2082
01:28:49,433 --> 01:28:51,600
Hey, he's got donuts
in his pockets.

2083
01:28:51,600 --> 01:28:54,233
Huh?
[Thunder rumbling]

2084
01:28:54,233 --> 01:28:55,833
Griffin.

2085
01:28:55,833 --> 01:28:58,400
Ran all the way to hell

2086
01:28:58,400 --> 01:29:01,867
with a penny
and a broken cigarette.

2087
01:29:01,867 --> 01:29:05,467
Which is really all you need
in hell, so it works out great.

2088
01:29:05,467 --> 01:29:07,467
Huzzah, it's gone!

2089
01:29:07,467 --> 01:29:10,333
I thought they portrayed 1961
quite well.

2090
01:29:10,333 --> 01:29:12,667
Hmm, not too hard,
since they made it in '65.

2091
01:29:12,667 --> 01:29:14,333
Doh! Psha!

2092
01:29:14,333 --> 01:29:16,200
♪ Night train ♪

2093
01:29:26,333 --> 01:29:30,633
[All groaning]

2094
01:29:30,633 --> 01:29:32,167
You know,
aside from the fact

2095
01:29:32,167 --> 01:29:35,300
that I'll never again
experience joy in my life,

2096
01:29:35,300 --> 01:29:36,933
I don't think
"red zone Cuba"

2097
01:29:36,933 --> 01:29:40,233
had any kind of negative effect
on me.

2098
01:29:40,233 --> 01:29:42,333
Yeah, even
being Carol Channing

2099
01:29:42,333 --> 01:29:44,200
didn't shield me from
the effects of this one.

2100
01:29:44,200 --> 01:29:45,800
[All sigh]

2101
01:29:45,800 --> 01:29:47,967
Well, hey, I know what we can do
to cheer ourselves up.

2102
01:29:47,967 --> 01:29:50,633
Let's sing us
a bouncy, upbeat song, okay?

2103
01:29:50,633 --> 01:29:52,200
- Okay.
- Okay, great idea!

2104
01:29:52,200 --> 01:29:53,500
Hit it, cambot!

2105
01:29:53,500 --> 01:29:56,033
♪♪
[all laughing]

2106
01:29:56,033 --> 01:29:58,000
Whoo! Yay!

2107
01:29:58,000 --> 01:30:01,067
♪ Oh, whenever I want to cry
and bawl ♪

2108
01:30:01,067 --> 01:30:03,700
- ♪ because I'm feeling sad ♪
- yeah?

2109
01:30:03,700 --> 01:30:06,667
♪ I think of
ironing boards and drywall ♪

2110
01:30:06,667 --> 01:30:09,500
♪ and then I don't
feel so bad ♪

2111
01:30:09,500 --> 01:30:12,133
♪ whenever
I'm feeling down and blue ♪

2112
01:30:12,133 --> 01:30:14,833
- ♪ and sorry for myself ♪
- uhh!

2113
01:30:14,833 --> 01:30:16,967
♪ I get some staples
and some glue ♪

2114
01:30:16,967 --> 01:30:19,833
- ♪ and I'm happy as an elf ♪
- [laughs]

2115
01:30:19,833 --> 01:30:22,767
♪ Whenever I start
to mope and pout ♪

2116
01:30:22,767 --> 01:30:25,167
♪ and there's nothing left
in my soul ♪

2117
01:30:25,167 --> 01:30:28,233
♪ I check the toilet paper
and if we're out ♪

2118
01:30:28,233 --> 01:30:31,000
♪ I buy another roll ♪

2119
01:30:31,000 --> 01:30:35,233
♪ have you ever
touched a post-it note ♪

2120
01:30:35,233 --> 01:30:38,833
♪ have you ever looked
at boots ♪

2121
01:30:38,833 --> 01:30:42,600
♪ have you ever
sat down in a chair ♪

2122
01:30:42,600 --> 01:30:48,133
♪ have you ever used
a paper clip ♪

2123
01:30:48,133 --> 01:30:50,500
♪ so if you listen
to our advice ♪

2124
01:30:50,500 --> 01:30:53,433
♪ and you wanna feel terrific ♪

2125
01:30:53,433 --> 01:30:55,800
♪ do things that make you
feel nice ♪

2126
01:30:55,800 --> 01:30:59,133
♪ I wish we could
be more specific ♪

2127
01:30:59,133 --> 01:31:02,033
[Groaning]

2128
01:31:02,033 --> 01:31:04,633
Ow! Oh! Oh! Agh!

2129
01:31:04,633 --> 01:31:06,433
Ohh! Ooh...

2130
01:31:06,433 --> 01:31:09,367
♪♪

2131
01:32:08,333 --> 01:32:11,267
♪♪ [Piano playing]

